{
  "analysis": "The freestanding test succeeded: the VM can execute compiler-generated MIPS I code and handle syscalls when we avoid glibc. Now I need to build full Doom freestanding. The main challenges are: (1) Doom uses many libc functions (malloc, printf, fopen, memcpy, etc.) that must be reimplemented via VM syscalls, (2) the VM only loads .text/.data/.rodata and starts at `main`, and (3) the WAD file must be found at /app/doom.wad.",
  "plan": "First, identify all libc functions used by Doom source. Then inspect doomgeneric_Create and WAD loading to understand argc/argv requirements. After that, create a libc shim and build the full freestanding MIPS binary.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "cd /app/doomgeneric/doomgeneric\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "grep -hoE '\\b(memset|memcpy|memmove|memcmp|malloc|free|calloc|realloc|printf|fprintf|sprintf|snprintf|vprintf|vsprintf|fopen|fclose|fwrite|fread|fseek|ftell|strlen|strcmp|strncmp|strcpy|strncpy|strcat|strncat|strchr|strrchr|strstr|strtol|strtoul|atoi|atof|toupper|tolower|sscanf|scanf|abort|exit|qsort|bsearch|time|clock|rand|srand|abs|labs|strncmp|stricmp|strnicmp|strcasecmp|strncasecmp)\\b' *.c | sort | uniq -c | sort -rn | head -80\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "grep -n \"doomgeneric_Create\" doomgeneric.c doomgeneric.h | head -20\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "sed -n '1,120p' doomgeneric.c\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "grep -n \"D_DoomMain\\|D_FindIWAD\\|D_FindFile\\|M_FindResponseFile\\|myargc\\|myargv\\|doomgeneric_Create\\|argc\\|argv\" d_main.c m_argv.c d_iwad.c | head -80\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    }
  ]
}
